# ledger/edits — what the compiler costs, measured by `wisp cost`
# accepted: list_reads +0.35% (check-cli; +0.40% check-program), empty_opens +0.15%, queries_computed +0.42% and peak_mb +0.25-0.40%: `@lacks` on the program layer, commit 'a field a record lacks on purpose' — each record's lacks asked once a program (`record_lacked`, one query a record) over its file's resolved `@lacks` rows (`file_lacks`, one a file), and its declaration laws reading only items that declare a record or an enum; bisected by commit at b6ec447a, the series and the side table at their base rows. Plus the law reads pins-3 adds: `guarded` read as a value (the name reads the generic-fn law reads) and a `select`'s arms judged against its first arm. The series' `SignedType.parameters` empty open is paid in its own commit.

